            <div xml:id="d649">

                <pb facs="0486" n="482" sameAs="frus:frus1938v04/pg482"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/13942: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Shanghai</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Gauss</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Shanghai</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-09-22T18:00:00+08:00">September 22, 1938—6
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 22—3:05 p.m.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1257. With reference to this Consulate General’s 1035, July 26<anchor n="97"
                        xml:id="d649-f1"/> concerning proposed Ichang safety zone, a written reply
                    was received today from the local Japanese Consulate General which states: <pb
                        facs="0487" n="483" xml:id="pg483"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Although the Japanese military authorities are unable to recognize
                            formally the proposed safety area, they are ready to give favorable
                            consideration to the matter insofar as it is not prejudicial to our
                            military operations, and at the same time so long as it is entirely
                            clear that the Chinese forces do not take advantage of, or approach the
                            proposed ‘safety area’.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <p>Repeated to Chungking, Tokyo, Hankow, by mail to Peiping.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gauss</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
